        "original_id": "b35fba49-3811-578b-bb24-ad481693bc7d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Havanese, Black Mouth Cur\n- Breed lineages: Bichon type, Blanquito de la Habana, Havana Silk Dogs\n- Places: Cuba, Havana, Southern United States\n\nFacts:\n- The Havanese is a dog breed of Bichon type.\n- The Havanese is the national dog of Cuba.\n- The Havanese was developed from the now extinct Blanquito de la Habana, which means \"little white dog of Havana.\"\n- Havana Silk Dogs was originally another name for the Blanquito de la Habana.\n- The Black Mouth Cur is a hunting and cattle dog.\n- The Black Mouth Cur originated in the Southern United States.",
